; The gate is OUTSIDE the smt/ stdlib-only firewall (I3), and stays lean: stdlib + Unix,
; no opam packages. It links exactly ONE module under smt/ — the shared SMT-LIB lexer
; oxsmt_lexical (ADR-0008) — so the token-boundary bug family is fixed once rather than in
; three divergent lexers. This narrows the DESIGN §10 N-version isolation at the LEXICAL
; layer only; the encoder and the Lean kernel (where oracle independence actually lives)
; link nothing else from smt/. Uncorrelated backstops: the fuzzer's cross-impl differential,
; Lean elaboration, and pre-labeled benchmarks (ADR-0008).

(executable
 (name gate)
 (libraries unix oxsmt_lexical))
